Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:20:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8450: keep the UFS PHY GDSC in retention

Use retention rather than ALWAYS_ON so CX can collapse. Retain flip-flops and poll CFG_GDSCR for the UFS PHY GDSC.

Source changes (original messages and trailers follow).

Source-commit: e94bd90d85f8ca1592f327f29810b17d826468ec
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-27T21:20:10+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0091-clk-qcom-gcc-sm8450-let-the-UFS-PHY-GDSC-power-off-a.patch

clk: qcom: gcc-sm8450: let the UFS PHY GDSC power off again

Drop the ALWAYS_ON flag that linux-marble c003e6341111 ("clk: qcom:
sm8450: poll USB GDSC and keep UFS PHY GDSC enabled") set on
UFS_PHY_GDSC; keep its USB30_PRIM_GDSC polling and retention flags.

The GCC GDSCs are now parented to RPMh CX, and the SM8475 UFS OPP table
votes CX through the UFS host's power domain (NOM for the node,
TURBO_L1 at 850 MHz). With UFS_PHY_GDSC always on, its genpd never
powered off, so the TURBO_L1 performance vote was never dropped and CX
stayed at that level through s2idle: on Marble the CX and DDR sleep
counters no longer advanced, where they did before this series.

ALWAYS_ON worked around UFS bus faults across power collapse. The SM8475
UFS series taken from Asphalt (full PHY tables, turbo configuration,
CX levels) together with no_phy_retention (spm_lvl 5) now powers the
UFS controller, device and PHY down in system suspend and fully
reinitialises them on resume; s2idle with spm_lvl 5 resumed cleanly on
Marble with that series, and 2 x 2 GiB writes and reads ran without
errors. Asphalt (SM8475) has never set this flag.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>

Source-commit: 98f3d7e17abac530be21f8369e6e6b31ff2bd879
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-27T21:50:34+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0092-clk-qcom-gcc-sm8450-poll-CFG_GDSCR-and-retain-flip-f.patch

clk: qcom: gcc-sm8450: poll CFG_GDSCR and retain flip-flops for the UFS PHY GDSC

Since the UFS PHY GDSC is no longer always on, it is powered off in
system suspend and switched back on by genpd in the noirq resume phase.
On a Xiaomi Poco F5 (SM7475, SM8475 GCC) every s2idle resume then warns
that the GDSC did not report its new state in time:

  ufs_phy_gdsc status stuck at 'off'
  WARNING: drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c:192 gdsc_toggle_logic
   gdsc_enable <- genpd_sync_power_on <- genpd_resume_noirq
  (triggered by the qcom-ice 1d88000.crypto resume)

UFS works afterwards and the SoC reaches CX collapse, but the power-up
handshake is not observed correctly. Like the USB30_PRIM_GDSC on this
board, and like ufs_phy_gdsc in the SM8550 (955f2ea3b9e9) and SM8650
(c58225b7e3d7) GCC drivers, poll the power status through CFG_GDSCR,
which reports the completed power-up/down sequence, and keep the
flip-flop state (RETAIN_FF_ENABLE) across the collapse.

Neither mainline nor linux-next (next-20261026) sets flags on the SM8450
ufs_phy_gdsc.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>

Source-commit: ef7319fc9e834f665188ec622d48b8e22172b5d2
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-28T22:32:44+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0093-clk-qcom-gcc-sm8450-keep-the-UFS-PHY-GDSC-in-retenti.patch

clk: qcom: gcc-sm8450: keep the UFS PHY GDSC in retention instead of off

Without ALWAYS_ON the UFS PHY GDSC is powered off in system suspend and
switched back on by genpd in the noirq resume phase. On a Xiaomi Poco F5
(SM7475, SM8475 GCC) every s2idle resume then warns:

  ufs_phy_gdsc status stuck at 'off'
  WARNING: drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c:192 gdsc_toggle_logic
   gdsc_enable <- genpd_sync_power_on <- genpd_resume_noirq
  (triggered by the qcom-ice 1d88000.crypto resume)

Polling CFG_GDSCR and retaining the flip-flops did not change this.

The SM8450/SM8475 UFS PHY GDSC supports retention; SM8550 and later do
not, which is why the UFS PHY GDSC is ALWAYS_ON there. Describe it as
PWRSTS_RET_ON: gdsc_disable() then leaves the GDSC on in hardware and it
enters retention when its parent CX collapses, so it is never switched
off and on by software. Unlike ALWAYS_ON, genpd still powers the domain
off and drops its vote on the parent CX domain, so CX can still collapse
in suspend. Keep POLL_CFG_GDSCR and RETAIN_FF_ENABLE; the latter keeps
the flip-flop state while the GDSC is in retention.

This follows the fix for "gcc_pcie_0_gdsc status stuck at 'off'" on
QCS8300, which moves the PCIe and USB GDSCs to PWRSTS_RET_ON.

Link: https://ratatoskr.run/linux-clk/2026/06/17190022/t
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c
index d77ab34224..a062b3ce9a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c
@@ -3133,8 +3133,8 @@ static struct gdsc ufs_phy_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "ufs_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = ALWAYS_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc usb30_prim_gdsc = {
